# Pi with a shell, POSIX tools and curl, and no compiler: the README's "Pi with npm",
# whose page installs four device host modules: display, input, download for
# the download tool of Pi's Dolly extension (Janis links its client), and html
# for its ask_user and show_html tools (the html command). The recipe engine
# lets an npm user build an image FROM it (dolly-build).
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-core 563a63e2105c57361dee073333471588559e2d0e0da6dbc9047cd6b7a066fc32
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-dollyfile 786fb12cb912ea545ff0f423d35f98f97a6da5d2a1b53d33481749827940b294
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-posix 3301750f545f28a9ea44a30dacc21adaa4ed6b2163a1e41e81bfabd621260d83
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-display c0429f7e9f403f4d2a65d8f5b90606eb815420a550d18936bedffd90c4fc702b
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-curl 5a3882d265b20fc066d1f8262b656f1266497e4644e8c7564437ac2e38ea99a1
